olution "Recall that if ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},$ and ${X}_{3}$ are mutually independent random variables, where \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}∼N({\\mu }_{1},{\\sigma }_{1}^{2}),\\,{X}_{2}∼N({\\mu }_{2},{\\sigma }_{2}^{2}),\\,{X}_{3}∼N({\\mu }_{3},{\\sigma }_{3}^{2}),\n$$\n\nthen \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Y & ={X}_{1}+{X}_{2}+{X}_{3} \\\\  & ∼N({\\mu }_{1}+{\\mu }_{2}+{\\mu }_{3},\\,{\\sigma }_{1}^{2}+{\\sigma }_{2}^{2}+{\\sigma }_{3}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{X}_{1}∼N(0,{3}^{2}),\\,{X}_{2}∼N(3,{2}^{2}),\\,{X}_{3}∼N(1,{2}^{2}),\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\nY={X}_{1}+{X}_{2}+{X}_{3}.\n$$\n\nSince ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},$ and ${X}_{3}$ are mutually independent, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y] & ={\\mu }_{1}+{\\mu }_{2}+{\\mu }_{3} \\\\  & =0+3+1 \\\\  & =4, \\\\ \\text{Var}[Y] & ={\\sigma }_{1}^{2}+{\\sigma }_{2}^{2}+{\\sigma }_{3}^{2} \\\\  & ={3}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{2}^{2} \\\\  & =9+4+4 \\\\  & =17.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Y={X}_{1}+{X}_{2}+{X}_{3} & ∼N(4,17).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186498517 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176012 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3414fb92-7c59-5e59-af67-5c57b75d759f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Distribution of a Sum of Normal Random Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "076d8d9d-6903-5544-8b75-42f7c2d31463" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Y∼N(-3,38)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497817} {:answer/id #uuid "68e234a9-c64f-5e7c-af28-388f7c1d4e9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Y∼N(-3,12)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498052} {:answer/id #uuid "6b2602de-e702-5c3c-8fe4-0a036fbcce6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Y∼N(5,38)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498060} {:answer/id #uuid "e8cf2b97-7282-5325-8d1e-46663f36e9b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident 